      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.8,
          "en": "So it's great that we're now storing meetups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.8,
          "end": 6.69,
          "en": "here in our collection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.69,
          "end": 9.58,
          "en": "but of course we're not using those stored meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.58,
          "end": 13.92,
          "en": "If we go to all meetups, I still display my dummy meetups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 16.41,
          "en": "the same for the details page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.41,
          "end": 21.41,
          "en": "Here we would now want to fetch data from mongodb as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.88,
          "end": 25.45,
          "en": "And of course we could now create new API routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.45,
          "end": 28.95,
          "en": "We could create an API route called meetups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 32.2,
          "en": "and in there, we add this handler function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.2,
          "end": 33.89,
          "en": "we connect to mongodb",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.89,
          "end": 37.89,
          "en": "and we then write code that fetches all the meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.89,
          "end": 42.38,
          "en": "And then on the starting page, in getStaticProps here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.38,
          "end": 44.98,
          "en": "we could simply use fetch()",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.98,
          "end": 47.84,
          "en": "and indeed nextJS adds a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.84,
          "end": 52.52,
          "en": "that you can use fetch() on server side code as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.52,
          "end": 55.03,
          "en": "Normally, you can only use it in the browser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 55.03,
          "end": 57.69,
          "en": "but in Next projects, you can use fetch()",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.69,
          "end": 60.67,
          "en": "in server side code snippets as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.67,
          "end": 62.63,
          "en": "And we could then use fetch() therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.63,
          "end": 65.47,
          "en": "to send the request to /api/meetups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.47,
          "end": 66.78,
          "en": "fetch all the meetups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.78,
          "end": 70.52,
          "en": "and then populate our props with those meetups.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.52,
          "end": 74.52,
          "en": "We could do that, but it would be a bit cumbersome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.52,
          "end": 78.08,
          "en": "Sending a request to our own API end point here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.08,
          "end": 79.99,
          "en": "is a bit redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.99,
          "end": 81.94,
          "en": "Keep in mind that I mentioned that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.94,
          "end": 85.02,
          "en": "the code you add here in getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.02,
          "end": 89.7,
          "en": "just as in getServerSideProps and getStaticProps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.7,
          "end": 93.93,
          "en": "will only run on the server or during build time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 93.93,
          "end": 95.97999999999999,
          "en": "but never in the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.97999999999999,
          "end": 100.49000000000001,
          "en": "So the code in here, will also not be exposed to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.49000000000001,
          "end": 103.18,
          "en": "So therefore here, if you wanna fetch all meet-ups,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.18,
          "end": 105.92,
          "en": "we can directly write the code for doing so",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.92,
          "end": 108.66,
          "en": "here inside of getStaticProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.66,
          "end": 112.50999999999999,
          "en": "or in a helper function, which we then execute here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.50999999999999,
          "end": 116.22,
          "en": "So we don't need to send the request to our own API route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.22,
          "end": 119.25999999999999,
          "en": "we can immediately execute the code just here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 119.25999999999999,
          "end": 122.67,
          "en": "which then writes this extra unnecessary requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.67,
          "end": 125.17,
          "en": "which would be sent otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.17,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "So therefore here we can, again import MongoClient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.41,
          "end": 139.29,
          "en": "from mongodb, and then connect to it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.29,
          "end": 143.48,
          "en": "Now, when you import something here in a page component file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.48,
          "end": 147.43,
          "en": "and that something is then only used in getServerSideProps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 147.43,
          "end": 152.41,
          "en": "or getStaticProps, the imported package will not be part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 152.41,
          "end": 154.6,
          "en": "of the client side bundle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.6,
          "end": 156.45,
          "en": "So you can import code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 156.45,
          "end": 159.112,
          "en": "which will then only be executed on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.112,
          "end": 161.716,
          "en": "and nextJS will detect this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 161.716,
          "end": 165.22,
          "en": "and not include it in your client's side bundle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.22,
          "end": 168.71,
          "en": "which is good both for bundle size considerations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 168.71,
          "end": 171.35,
          "en": "as well as for security.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 171.35,
          "end": 173.69,
          "en": "So you can import both server side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 173.69,
          "end": 175.07999999999998,
          "en": "and clients side code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 177.09,
          "en": "and depending on where you use it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.09,
          "end": 179.88,
          "en": "it will be included in different bundles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.88,
          "end": 182.34,
          "en": "which are independent from each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.34,
          "end": 185.433,
          "en": "That's a nice, smart feature built into nextJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.049,
          "end": 189.93,
          "en": "And therefore with MongoClient import here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.93,
          "end": 193.493,
          "en": "We can use it in getStaticProps to again connect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.77,
          "end": 198.13,
          "en": "And now we can go to the API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 198.13,
          "end": 200.75,
          "en": "and get rid of meetups.js there by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.75,
          "end": 204.39,
          "en": "and the new-meetup.js we can now in the end copy this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.39,
          "end": 206.74,
          "en": "for establishing connection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.74,
          "end": 208.19,
          "en": "getting access to the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.19,
          "end": 210.32,
          "en": "and getting access to a collection here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.32,
          "end": 212.5,
          "en": "We could therefore also refactor this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.5,
          "end": 214.89,
